&Q000546 = Letter from Puzur-Šulgi to Šulgi about the advance of the enemy
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.1.07
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.1.07&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. lugal-ŋu₁₀-ra u₃-na-a-dug₄
#tr.en: Say to my lord: this is what @varh[t3107.v1]{@wPN{Puzur-@wRN{Šulgi}} } @vart[t3107.v2,t3107.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} @wPN{Puzur-@wDN{Marduk}} } @vart[t3107.v3,t3107.v1]{@varn{1 other ms. has instead:} @wPN{Puzur-@wDN{Numušda}} }, the commander of the fortress @wGN{Igi-ḫursaŋa}, your servant, says:
#lem: lugal[king]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. (1:puzur₄-{d}šul-gi:1) šagina bad₃ igi-hur-saŋ-ŋa₂
#lem: Puzuršulgir[1]PN; šakkanak[general]; bad[wall]; Igihursaŋa[1]GN
#etcsl: line-id=2

:2v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) puzur₄-{d}marduk
#lem: Puzurmarduk[1]PN
:2v.1.2: ($1 other ms. has instead:$) puzur₄-{d}nu-muš#-[da]
#lem: Puzurnumušda[1]PN

3. arad-zu na-ab-be₂-a
#lem: arad[slave]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. lugal-ŋu₁₀ (1:kug-sig₁₇ kug-babbar:1) (2:diŋir-re-e-ne:2) in-ne-dim₂-dim₂-ma
#tr.en: All the @varh[t3107.v4]{gold and silver } @vart[t3107.v5,t3107.v4]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} gold and lapis lazuli } @vart[t3107.v6,t3107.v4]{@varn{1 other ms. has instead:} silver and gold } that my lord
#lem: lugal[king]; kugsig[gold]; kugbabbar[silver]; diŋir[deity]; dim[create]
#etcsl: line-id=4

:4v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) kug-sig₁₇ {na₄}za-gin₃
#lem: kugsig[gold]; zagin[lapis lazuli]
:4v.1.2: ($1 other ms. has instead:$) kug-babbar kug-sig₁₇#
#lem: kugbabbar[silver]; kugsig[gold]
:4v.2.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) diŋir gal-gal
#lem: diŋir[deity]; gal[big]

5. zi-ni-še₃-am₃ in-nu-u₃
#tr.en: has been fashioning for the @vart[t3107.v7,t3107.v7]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} great } gods -- is it not for his own life?
#lem: zi[life]; nu[not]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. lugal-ŋu₁₀ (1:zi:1) ugnim u₃ kalam-ma-ni-še₃
#tr.en: For @varh[t3107.v8]{the life } @vart[t3107.v9,t3107.v8]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} the well-being } of the troops and his land,
#lem: lugal[king]; zi[life]; ugnim[army]; u[and]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]
#etcsl: line-id=6

:6v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) silim-ma
#lem: silim[healthy]

7. bad₃ gal igi-hur-saŋ-ŋa₂ mu lu₂-kur₂ hul-ŋal₂-še₃
#tr.en: my king has built the great fortress @wGN{Igi-ḫursaŋa} for the people of his land,
#lem: bad[wall]; gal[big]; Igihursaŋa[1]GN; mu[name]; lukur[stranger]; huluŋal[evil]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. uŋ₃ kalam-ma-ni-še₃ mu-un-du₃
#tr.en: because of the wicked enemy.
#lem: uŋ[people]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; du[build]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. i₃-ne-eš ugnim lu₂-kur₂-ra im-ma-an-zig₃
#tr.en: And now the enemy troops have risen up.
#lem: ineš[now]; ugnim[army]; lukur[stranger]; zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. (1:1-am₃:1) lu₂ igi-ŋa₂ sah₆-bi i-im-tum₂-ma dab₅-dab₅-be₂
#tr.en: @varh[t3107.v10]{One } @vart[t3107.v11,t3107.v10]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} …… } man who had fled from me has been brought back.
#lem: n; lu[person]; igi[eye]; zah[disappear]; tum[bring]; dab[seize]
#etcsl: line-id=10

:10v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) [...]-ni#-am₃
#lem: X

11. inim ma-an-dug₄-ma (1:igi-še₃! ib-DU:1)
#tr.en: Having been caught, he has given me evidence of this, and @varh[t3107.v12]{went ahead } @vart[t3107.v13,t3107.v12]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} @q{“…… go!”}, and I (?) went }.
#lem: inim[word]; dug[speak]; igi[eye]; X
#etcsl: line-id=11

:11v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) [...]-ŋen-na-ab ba-ŋen
#lem: ŋen[go]; ŋen[go]

12. ŋiškim lu₂-kur₂-ra ŋe₂₆-e i₃-zu
#tr.en: I am also well-informed about the oracular signs concerning the enemy: the enemy has replenished his strength for battle.
#lem: ŋeškim[sign]; lukur[stranger]; ŋaʾe[I]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. lu₂-kur₂ me₃!-še₃ usu-ni im-ma-til usu-ŋu₁₀ i₃-tur
#tr.en: However, my strength is limited.
#lem: lukur[stranger]; me[battle]; usu[strength]; til[complete]; usu[strength]; tur[small]
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. bad₃ nu-mu-un-da-kal-la-ge (1:en-nu nu-mu-da-ak-e:1)
#tr.en: I cannot strengthen the fortress further or @varh[t3107.v14]{guard it } @vart[t3107.v15,t3107.v14]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} guard the cities (?) } against him.
#lem: bad[wall]; kalag[strong]; ennuŋ[watch]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=14

:14v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) iri# en-<nu> nu-un-da-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
